  "@id": "https://pices-data.github.io/odis/records/zenodo-23569228.jsonld",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Plankton Data from the Central Bering Sea and Gulf of Alaska Sampled by the R/V Kaiyo maru during the Summer and Fall 2003",
  "description": "Plankton data were collected in the central Bering Sea and Gulf of Alaska by the Japanese R/V Kaiyo maru from June to September 2003. The R/V Kaiyo maru sampled plankton at every station at the approximate location of the trawl tows. Zooplankton were collected using a NORPAC net at each trawl station (daytime sampling only). At nighttime, bongo and RMT (multi-layer) nets were used for zooplankton sampling. The bongo net was towed between the surface and 100 m. The RMT net was towed from about 500 m to the surface. The RMT net was also used for diel sampling. Plankton were sampled by RMT net at six depth layers from 500 m to surface: 500 - 300 m, 300 - 200 m, 200 - 100 m, 100 - 50 m, 50 - 25 m, and 25 - 0 m. Sea surface particle size of plankton and fluorescence were measured continuously by Electronic Particle Counting and Sizing System (EPCS). The fluorescence and number of particles correspond to the phytoplankton biomass and zooplankton biomass, respectively.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To collect plankton as part of the BASIS survey of the Bering Sea.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23569229",
